    "description": "## Outcome and context\n\nEmily asked us to confirm Survey Completed Date is populated from SLC/CMS data, and if so, that reps shouldn't be able to edit it — only Ops.\n\n## Current state\n\nBUILD-69 (WAGR-46) confirms Survey Completed Date (Date_Survey_Completed__c) is populated by an inbound CMS→Salesforce event (player external id + completed_at), replacing the earlier click-inference logic. No field-level security restriction limiting edit access to Ops has been scoped or built.\n\n## Proposed solution\n\n1. Confirm to Emily that Survey Completed Date is system-populated per BUILD-69.\n2. Set field-level security on Date_Survey_Completed__c (and the related Survey_Completed__c checkbox, if applicable) so the field is read-only for the Rep profile/permission set and editable only for Ops.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. A user on the WT Rep permission set cannot edit Survey Completed Date.\n2. An Ops user can edit it when a correction is needed.\n3. The CMS-driven automation (BUILD-69) continues to populate the field without being blocked by the FLS change.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nDepends on BUILD-69 — Survey completion inbound API event → Player (WAGR-46).\n\n## Source\n\nWagertech Notes / Questions (Emily Vandenberg), Player record doc, reviewed Sep 2026: \"Confirming that Survey Completed Date is populated based on the SLC data — If yes, the rep should not be able to edit, just Ops.\" https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mp3b1qpJkzKNDztEQpdnv-BYCgUgDdXe5jLuJi-ix1U/edit?tab=t.0",
